00:16:51,600 --> 00:16:57,200
Yeah, so Indiegogo and Kickstarter, that is, you know, that is a form of crowdfunding, I suppose.

203
00:16:57,680 --> 00:17:00,800
Uh, but you're, you know, the quote unquote investors are backers, right?

204
00:17:01,040 --> 00:17:09,920
They back this product and by giving some money, you effectively donate the money, you might get that product sooner than anybody else, but you're not investing in the business.

205
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:12,400
So you're not getting an equity share of the business.

206
00:17:13,040 --> 00:17:19,840
So there are platforms, uh, here in the UK with Cedars, who's since been bought by Republic from the US, uh, CrowdCube.

207
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:21,680
There's a bunch of different ones across the world.

208
00:17:22,320 --> 00:17:24,560
And it's basically you're investing.

209
00:17:25,840 --> 00:17:27,680
your money and you get a share of the business.

210
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:36,480
Now the platform usually sits on the cap table and becomes your front of the investors of Activity because you have a long tail.

211
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:39,840
We have 2,500 investors like this by now.

212
00:17:40,960 --> 00:17:42,800
But yeah, anybody can invest, right?

213
00:17:42,960 --> 00:17:50,640
And so anybody can invest as little as ten bucks or as much as hundreds of thousands if they want to.

214
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:53,200
So when we started, we weren't sure what was going to happen.

